From 352ebc043e89f5a4473cc36414adced6ca7f9e8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 16:22:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03303/11362] [outer-loop] arc: transition-capture sink +
 human-replay ingestion (14.6k-transition corpus)

Operator directive (2026-06-21): capture gameplay for learning/training, augmenting the human-recorded
play datasets. We were discarding every transition (recordings empty; collect_transitions on-demand).

python/carnot/agentic/arc_transition_capture.py:
- TransitionCorpus: append-only, deduped per-game npz store of (game, grid, action, data, next_grid,
  level_before, level_after) under data/arc_transition_corpus/ (gitignored; regenerable). add/flush/load/
  stats round-trip validated.
- capture_public_games(): offline-arcade probe over the 25 public games -> corpus.
- ingest_human_replays(): folds the HUMAN play corpus (data/arc_public_demo_human_replay_corpus,
  frame_action_delta.v1, ~14,797 rows / 25 games, CC BY 4.0) by pairing consecutive frames per session
  guid into transitions; robust to int|'ACTIONn' action ids; level-up flagged on level_progress reset.

Result: 14,628 transitions across all 25 public games, OVERWHELMINGLY state-changing (human play is
goal-directed -- e.g. wa30 1532/1545, lf52 1210/1210 changing) vs the no-op-dominated random probes. This
is the high-signal fuel for the pretrained mechanic PRIOR (the 25 public games are our only window into
the mechanic distribution the hidden eval is drawn from; we cannot capture the hidden games -- learn, not
memorize). 3.4MB compressed.

NEXT (the remaining two of the three): turn on live-session recording in arc3_live_submit (feed the sink
+ debug trail), then the pretrain-prior path (dynamics backbone on this corpus -> LiveTTTWorldModel
warm-start -> measure transfer on held-out public games).

